{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the assembly was gathered to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting.</b> It was a miraculous event, and this is one of the places where the small held the many. Like it (Numbers 20:10): ״ויקהילו משה ואהרן את הקהל אל פני הסלע״. And so they said in the Midrash — ״ואת כל העדה הקהל אל פתח אהל מועד״: Moses said before Him, Master of the universe, six hundred thousand men and six hundred thousand youths — how can I stand them at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting? He said to him, the Holy One, blessed be He: at this you marvel? Behold, the heavens are like the film of an eye, and I stretch them from one end of the world to the other, as it is said (Isaiah 40:22): ״הנוטה כדוק שמים וימתחם כאהל לשבת״. And likewise at Mount Sinai, the Holy One, blessed be He, revealed Himself upon Mount Sinai with twenty-two thousand chariots of ministering angels, as it is said (Psalms 68:18): ״רכב אלהים רבותים אלפי שנאן״ — and each and every chariot was like the chariot that Ezekiel saw — and how could the mountain hold them all? Rather, it was a miracle: the Holy One, blessed be He, would say to the mountain, Expand! and it would receive the faithful. And once they crossed the Jordan, all Israel entered between the two staves of the Ark, as it is said (Joshua 3:9): ״ויאמר יהושע אל בני ישראל גשו הנה ושמעו את דברי יהוה אלהיכם״. And likewise in the future, all those multitudes that came forth from the first Adam until the dead come back to life — where will they stand? And they are destined to say (Isaiah 49:20): ״צר לי המקום גשה לי ואשבה״ — rather, I will broaden Jerusalem, as it is said (ibid. 54 — 'הרחיבי מקום אהלך ויריעות משכנותיך'), and it is written (Ezekiel 41:7): ״ורחבה ונסבה למעלה למעלה״ — this far in the Midrash."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:57.181034765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}